{"name":"Hog-Maw","hex":"#fbe8e4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any animal belonging to the Suidae family of mammals, especially the pig, the warthog, and the boar.\n An adult swine, at or above a certain body weight.","An adult swine, at or above a certain body weight."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To greedily take more than one's share, to take precedence at the expense of another or others.","To clip the mane of a horse, making it short and bristly.\n\n (of a hedge) to trim up closely"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hog"},{"term":"maw","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mampruli."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The upper digestive tract (where food enters the body), especially the mouth and jaws of an animal.\n\n The mouth and jaws of a furry.","The mouth and jaws of a furry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maw"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hog maw","blocks":[{"text":"Hog maw is the stomach of a pig prepared as food. More specifically, it is the exterior muscular wall of the stomach organ which contains no fat if cleaned properly. It can be found in American, soul food, Chinese, Pennsylvania Dutch, Mexican, German, Portuguese, Italian and Vietnamese dishes. In addition, it can be prepared in various ways including stewed, fried, baked, and broiled."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Hog_maw.jpg/330px-Hog_maw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hog_maw","wikidata":"Q5650138"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Hog_maw_with_pork_and_beef_dumplings-2010-19-01.jpg/500px-Hog_maw_with_pork_and_beef_dumplings-2010-19-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Hog_maw_with_p